      "id": "089490a9d765189a0e27",
      "title": "AI let's you scale. But what about the accessibility debt? READ REPORTS",
      "location": null,
      "url": "https://accessibe.com/accessibility-platform/reports/gen-ai-ecommerce",
      "description": "Accessibility & eCommerce Insights | accessiBe Skip to content AI is scaling your storefront. But is accessibility keeping pace? Get key insights on how eCommerce and DTC brands are scaling with generative AI — and what it takes to stay accessible while they grow Gen AI in eComm: the rewards and the accessibility debt 78% of eCommerce brands now generate more than a quarter of their content with AI, and trust in it runs high — a level of speed and confidence most teams could only aim for a few years ago. Accessibility, though, is proving to be the harder half of the equation. Among brands that have faced accessibility legal action, 65.4% point to AI-generated content as the top-cited factor. These reports map the areas in which accessibility gaps most commonly occur, showcase what those gaps look like on real, audited storefronts, and offer practical steps you can take to stay ahead. Discover key insights: 78% of brands now generate a quarter of their content with AI AI isn't a pilot project anymore — it's core infrastructure. See exactly where it's showing up across the storefront. Read more 82.5% of eComm leaders worry AI content is creating unseen barriers From adaptive layouts to alt text, see exactly where AI-generated content breaks for shoppers with disabilities Read more AI-generated content - now the top-cited factor in accessibility lawsuits See where legal risk is concentrating, and how these cases are actually resolving Read more 51% of brands say AI accessibility ownership defaults to engineering Confidence in the process runs high — but ownership is inherited, not assigned. See where the gap opens up Read more Two AI-built storefronts. 24 accessibility issues between them. We audited two AI-built storefronts. See what prompts can—and can’t—fix. Read more 62.3% of brands name AI accessibility their top priority for the next year See the four ownership models for building a real AI accessibility program, and how to pick the right on